<title>USA: Georgia Power 900 MW unit back in service.</title>
<headline>Georgia Power 900 MW unit back in service.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 900 megawatt (MW) coal-fired power unit at Georgia Power Co's Scherer generating plant in Juliette, Ga., was operating at full power Thursday after returning from a maintenance outage begun Sept 16, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;All four units at Scherer are up and running,&quot; the spokeswoman said Thursday.</p>
<p>The Scherer plant is made up of four, 900 megawatt units.</p>
<p>Georgia Power is a subsidiary of Southern Co.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
